## 4. User Interface & Indicators

### Hardware Switches
* **Power Switch:** Controls the main power state of the base station.
* **Arming Switch:** Arms the recovery system and turns on the Armed LED to confirm status, enabling parachute deployment commands to go live.

### Status LEDs
| LED | Function |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Armed LED** | Illuminates when the arming switch has been actuated and the system has confirmed an armed state, signaling that parachute deployment commands are now live. |
| **Data LED** | Pulses/illuminates on receipt of valid telemetry packets from the Flight Computer, giving the operator a visual heartbeat of the downlink. |
| **Connection LED** | Indicates that a valid wireless link (XBee association) is established between the base station and the Flight Computer. |
| **4th LED** | Reserved/spare status indicator for additional fault or mode signaling. |

### Keypad Mapping (3x4 Matrix Keypad)
| Key | Action | Functionality |
| :---: | :--- | :--- |
| **0** | HELP | Prints full list of commands/key mapping to the laptop via Serial. |
| **1** | ARM | Arms the ESP32. |
| **2** | DISARM | Disarms the ESP32. |
| **3** | RESET | Sends Reset command to ESP32. |
| **4** | MAIN ON | Turns on main chute deployment. |
| **5** | MAIN OFF | Turns off main chute deployment. |
| **6** | Page Cycle | Cycles the LCD display through its 4 pages: `PAGE_MAIN` → `PAGE_ALT` → `PAGE_GPS` → `PAGE_PYRO` → back to `PAGE_MAIN`. Clears and redraws the LCD. |
| **7** | DROGUE_ON | Turns on drogue chute deployment. |
| **8** | DROGUE_OFF | Turns off drogue chute deployment. |
| **9** | STATUS | Prints a status string to the laptop over USB serial (Shows `"STATUS->USB"` on LCD row 3). |
| **\*** | XBee Toggle | Toggles a local boolean (`xbeeOnLocal`) and sends either `XBEE_ON` or `XBEE_OFF` to the ESP32 depending on the new state. *Note: this toggle is purely local and can desync if a command fails.* |
| **#** | Clear LCD | Clears the LCD screen and forces a full redraw of the current page. |

### LCD Display
A 16x2-character LCD display with an I2C interface module provides at-a-glance status information (e.g., link status, armed state, battery level) directly on the base station enclosure.

